From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:38:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] split renderer: expand strips and fans on the walker's
 thread; vitaGL redundant-state switch

- Renderer::prepare_draw(): work on a draw that needs only the draw. The
  GL renderer turns a transformed triangle strip or fan into the triangle
  list submit() would build (triangle_indices order); SplitRenderer calls it
  on the walker's thread in submit_taking(), so the GL thread only rebases the
  indices (ARM count of the GL thread's work: 3.0 -> 2.6 million
  instructions a frame). ge_replay --prepare does the same in the replay.
- The viewport memo compares its key field by field (no key array).
- GlSettings::vgl_skip_redundant (GL_VGL_SKIP_REDUNDANT, off): calls
  vglSkipRedundantState, which a vitaGL with the port's patch 0003 has
  (PORTABLEKIT_VITAGL_SKIP_REDUNDANT); nothing without it.

Verified: 25 replayed gameplay frames byte-identical with --prepare and
without; Vita3K: mission 1 with the split renderer and the vitaGL switch on
drew menus, movies, the briefing and gameplay correctly. Not yet on a Vita.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h b/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h
index ae449db..607a81d 100644
--- a/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h
+++ b/host/gpu/gl/gl_platform.h
@@ -82,6 +82,15 @@ inline void buffer_use_mapped(GLenum target, const void *data) {
 #endif
 }
 
+// vitaGL (the port's patch 0003): leave out GXM state calls that set what is already set. Nothing elsewhere.
+inline void skip_redundant_state(bool on) {
+#if defined(__vita__) && defined(PORTABLEKIT_VITAGL_SKIP_REDUNDANT)
+    vglSkipRedundantState(on ? GL_TRUE : GL_FALSE);
+#else
+    (void)on;
+#endif
+}
+
 inline void disable_dither() {
 #if !defined(__vita__)
     glDisable(GL_DITHER);
